---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[manual_clamp]: `x` is kept between `0` and `100` by hand
  --> tests/lint/manual_clamp/bad.jai:8:10
   |
 8 |     a := max(0, min(100, x));
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `clamp(x, 0, 100)`
   |
 8 ~     a := clamp(x, 0, 100);
   |
   = note: `manual_clamp` is `warn` by default

warning[manual_clamp]: `x` is kept between `0` and `LIMIT` by hand
  --> tests/lint/manual_clamp/bad.jai:9:10
   |
 9 |     b := min(LIMIT, max(0, x));
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `clamp(x, 0, LIMIT)`
   |
 9 ~     b := clamp(x, 0, LIMIT);
   |
   = note: `manual_clamp` is `warn` by default

warning[manual_clamp]: `x` is kept between `0` and `100` by hand
  --> tests/lint/manual_clamp/bad.jai:10:10
   |
10 |     c := max(min(100, x), 0);
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `clamp(x, 0, 100)`
   |
10 ~     c := clamp(x, 0, 100);
   |
   = note: `manual_clamp` is `warn` by default

warning[manual_clamp]: `f` is kept between `0.0` and `1.0` by hand
  --> tests/lint/manual_clamp/bad.jai:11:10
   |
11 |     d := max(0.0, min(1.0, f));
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `clamp(f, 0.0, 1.0)`
